&lt;h2&gt;What is AEO vs. AI visibility? (And why it matters)&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AEO&lt;/strong&gt; stands for &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/answer-engine-optimization"&gt;answer engine optimization&lt;/a&gt;, and it’s the practice of creating and modifying online content so that it is more likely to be mentioned and cited by AI answer engines like ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini. You might also hear people refer to AEO as GEO (&lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/generative-engine-optimization"&gt;generative engine optimization&lt;/a&gt;) or AI SEO, but here at HubSpot, we stick with the term AEO.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AEO matters because, as AI becomes more popular, people are turning to answer engines to do their buyer research, in addition to Google. In 2026, nearly half of U.S. adults use AI chatbots, up from one-third in 2024, according to the &lt;a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/internet/2026/06/17/americans-and-ai-2026-chatbots-smart-devices-and-views-on-impact/"&gt;Pew Research Center&lt;/a&gt;. Further, Pew found that 60% of American adults read the AI-generated summaries at the top of search results, while only 30% say they do not. Brands that learn and leverage AEO will gain a competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI visibility&lt;/strong&gt; is an umbrella term for the metrics that measure how your brand shows up in AI search, including share of voice, sentiment, citations, and mentions. It matters because this is how marketers and SEOs track their AEO progress.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro tip: &lt;/strong&gt;To get a baseline snapshot of your AI visibility, use the free &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/aeo-grader"&gt;AI Search Grader&lt;/a&gt; tool.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prompts&lt;/strong&gt; are to AEO what keywords are to SEO. Prompts are the phrases that users type into answer engines to get information about their query. Marketers use AEO tools like HubSpot AEO to track the prompts their brands should show up for.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Citations&lt;/strong&gt; are the websites that the AI consulted to generate its answer. They may or may not be linked.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coverage&lt;/strong&gt; is shorthand for “answer engine coverage,” which refers to which LLMs the AEO tool tracks. For example, HubSpot AEO covers ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;HubSpot AEO vs. Semrush AI Visibility: Core Comparison&lt;/h2&gt; 
